.TH kannadi-normalize 1  "normalize 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
kannadi\-normalize \- Normalize Unicode Kannada text, following the Kannada text normalization profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkannadi normalize\fR [\fB\-\-form\fR] [\fB\-\-stats\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIINPUTS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Normalize Unicode Kannada text, following the Kannada text normalization profile
.PP
Reads UTF\-8 text files, or standard input, and writes the normalized text to standard output. canonical gives 1 spelling to text that renders the same; legacy also repairs mistakes of legacy font converters and OCR, such as a zero typed for anusvara; search also folds Old Kannada letters, joiners and the nukta, for search keys. NORMALIZATION.md in the kannadi repository lists every rule.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-form\fR \fI<FORM>\fR [default: canonical]
How far to go
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
canonical
.IP \(bu 2
legacy
.IP \(bu 2
search
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\fR
Print how many times each rule changed the text to standard error, as TSV
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Write nothing; exit with status 1 if any input is not already in the form
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIINPUTS\fR]
UTF\-8 text files; standard input when none is given or for \-
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  kannadi normalize page.txt > page.normalized.txt
  kannadi normalize \-\-form legacy \-\-stats converted.txt > clean.txt
  kannadi normalize \-\-check corpus/*.txt

Exit status:
  0  Success.
  1  \-\-check was given and an input is not in the form.
  2  A file could not be read or is not UTF\-8.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
